      "card_ids": ["C19"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Ondansetron, a carbazole-containing drug, has absolute oral bioavailability of 50–65% in fasted volunteers and 40% after rifampin pretreatment, supporting that this scaffold can achieve F ≥ 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C01", "C03", "C20", "C28"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The low absolute bioavailability of penicillin V in fasted pigs (18.9 ± 4.8%) is not transferable to the query because the query is not a beta-lactam and the record is species- and molecule-specific.",
