      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C21", "C23", "C26", "C27", "C29"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental oral bioavailability data are available for the query molecule itself.",
    "The LCS1269 record is a predicted HIA-based value rather than a measured absolute bioavailability.",
    "Vinorelbine and ondansetron are structural analogs with different scaffolds/substituents; transfer is indirect.",
    "The low penicillin V pig bioavailability is not structurally transferable to the query.",
    "No query-specific solubility, permeability, or first-pass clearance data are available.",
    "The query formulation is unspecified, and vinorelbine data show formulation-dependent F values."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Although the physicochemical prior is low, all transferable structural analog evidence — vinorelbine (F ≈ 40%), LCS1269 (predicted F > 30%), and ondansetron (F ≈ 50–65%, 40% after rifampin) — supports F ≥ 20%. The new L2 records do not provide query-specific low-F evidence; the low penicillin V pig value is not transferable, so the prediction remains high."
}

